# One rule for line endings, enforced by git rather than by whoever edits
# next. Every text file is stored with LF and checked out with LF, on
# every platform — including Windows, which is the only platform this app
# runs on. Without this the repo drifts into a mix, and any tool that
# rewrites a file whole normalizes it to whatever it feels like, so a
# two-line change arrives as a nine-hundred-line diff and the real edit is
# impossible to see in review.
#
# LF rather than CRLF because that is what CI builds and lints with, and
# what every Rust toolchain emits; git for Windows and every editor in use
# here read LF without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images and icons are binary: never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
